``` LF-11 | Forwarders Pinned to One Indexer: Uneven Load Balancing
    Splunk Administrator Field Manual - Gaurav Malik

    Use case: Some indexers are much busier than others or fill their disks
    first; measure how evenly forwarder traffic spreads across the indexers
    and find forwarders that stick to a single indexer.
    Run on: SH. host is the receiving indexer; fwd is the forwarder.
    Query: Share of total ingest per indexer (SH)
    If this returns nothing, run probes/LF-11-probe.spl to confirm the data it
    reads exists here.
```
index=_internal source=*metrics.log group=tcpin_connections earliest=-4h
| stats sum(kb) as kb dc(hostname) as forwarders by host
| eventstats sum(kb) as total_kb
| eval pct_of_ingest=round(100 * kb / total_kb, 1),
       gb=round(kb / 1024 / 1024, 2)
| sort - pct_of_ingest
| table host forwarders gb pct_of_ingest
